# Google service-account keys. NEVER commit one.
#
# This repo is public (see functions/.gitignore), and a key with Firestore
# write access in a public repo is a total compromise of the economy: anyone
# who finds it can set any balance, approve any payout, and read every user
# document. The patterns are broad on purpose - a key saved under a name
# nobody predicted is exactly how this goes wrong.
*serviceaccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json
gcloud-key.json
# The short names a key gets renamed to once somebody is tired of typing the
# one Google generated. "*-adminsdk-*.json" catches the download as it comes
# out of the console and nothing after that.
key.json
*-key.json
adc.json
application_default_credentials.json
credentials.json
/secrets/
